      "value": "Brochure printed in black ink on glossy paper including information about film screenings, sponsors, and seminars. A dedication to the singer-actor-athlete-activist Paul Robeson, who passed away in January 1976, is included. Advertisements cover a range of topics, including Dr. Samella Lewis and Ruth Waddy's Black Artists on Art, Elizabeth Catlett's Louis Armstrong sculpture, Los Angeles Street Graphics, The Speakeasy, Casablanca Records, and Chocolate City Records."
